// Lightweight join transition: reuse the polished splash overlay as a short, non-blocking
// "joining → confirmed" moment. It is pointer-events:none so it never blocks the app, and
// only reflects backend-confirmed success/failure (no faked success). Native rebuild note:
// the future Swift app can replace this with a native transition (e.g. the L/U mark coming
// together + a LineUp-blue glow) — this web overlay is the product reference, not the impl.
function showJoinTransition(text){var s=$("#splash");if(!s)return;var t=s.querySelector(".splash-tagline");if(t)t.textContent=text;s.style.display="flex";s.style.pointerEvents="none";s.classList.remove("out")}
